{
  "summary": "This experiment tested weighted fusion in place of concat fusion, holding all other variables identical to llm_summary_006 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50), yielding a validation accuracy of ~0.678 (F1: ~0.646) compared to ~0.632 (F1: ~0.607) under concat. In this clean single-variable comparison, weighted fusion improved accuracy by approximately 0.046 and exceeded the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline of ~0.650 (llm_summary_005), indicating that the ResNet50 image branch does carry complementary signal that was being diluted by unweighted concatenation. It remains uncertain whether stronger image encoders (e.g., ViT-L), alternative fusion mechanisms (e.g., gating or attention), or different weighting schemes could yield further gains beyond the current 0.678, and whether the residual improvement over the RNA-only baseline reflects meaningful multimodal headroom or is largely attributable to the weighted mechanism downweighting a still-weak image feature (0.208 alone)."
}

